From 70debed9521bc6bfdbed5cda8b08aa4e69ff203f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 06:28:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] dt-bindings: spmi: apple,spmi: Add t6050 compatible

The T6050 (M5 Pro/Max) SPMI controllers are the T8142 generation-4
controller: the T6050 device trees describe their nub-spmi buses as
"apple,t6050-spmi", "apple,t8142-spmi", and spmi-apple-controller
drives them through the T8142 entry (the J716s Type-C controllers sit
on one). Allow that pair.

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM Claude
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/spmi/apple,spmi.yaml | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/spmi/apple,spmi.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/spmi/apple,spmi.yaml
index 0b35a017bb80..c7e057262696 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/spmi/apple,spmi.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/spmi/apple,spmi.yaml
@@ -36,6 +36,9 @@ properties:
               - apple,t6000-spmi
               - apple,t8112-spmi
           - const: apple,spmi
+      - items:
+          - const: apple,t6050-spmi
+          - const: apple,t8142-spmi
       - const: apple,t8142-spmi
 
   reg:
-- 
